{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: make a link in a record to that record's signed evidence attachment open the attachment preview. Take this after the current #21223 documentation correction and landing, before #20047; this is a small follow-up to Hugh's requirement for clickable file references and a useful preview surface. Preserve the remaining queue.\n\nConfirmed on the delivered b23 reader: #21221 has a Markdown link labelled current reader baseline whose destination is rollout-baseline.json. Clicking it in the actual owned IAB opens a source-file target and reports that the file is absent at b23. Clicking the same record's listed evidence attachment opens all 150 lines successfully. I independently reproduced the two API targets; the attachment exists and the repository file does not. The paired responses and operator's actual browser record are in this request's evidence list. #21229 records successful reader replacement and separately discloses this navigation defect; no reader restart or historical rollout replay is part of this source task.\n\nThe current [record detail](ui/src/components/RecordDetail.tsx@b23c0263033b1d57e7a493d7c30b1ea6c53b980c:78) renders statement text and body values without attachment names, while its evidence list loads them separately. The shared [reference renderer](ui/src/components/Preview.tsx@b23c0263033b1d57e7a493d7c30b1ea6c53b980c:15) already distinguishes a named attachment when given that information. Use one coherent, bounded resolution path so a reader need not know whether to click the prose or the evidence row. These are current live published behavior bases with ordinary inherited staleness and no superseded-world flag.\n\nDeliver the full narrow outcome: inline Markdown links, recognizable file mentions and body-value links to an attachment belonging to the displayed record resolve consistently with its evidence list; ordinary source links, explicit commit/line links, standalone Notes, and browser history continue to work. Define and test the case where source and evidence share a name so the target is deterministic and the source remains reachable; do not silently guess another event, another revision, or an external file. Handle loading, failure and record switching without briefly binding a link to the previous record's evidence. Reuse bounded per-record metadata; do not fetch once per token or scan whole history. Preserve size/window/path and untrusted-Markdown restrictions.\n\nProve the failing example through the actual component/interaction route, including a same-name source/attachment case, missing attachment, rapid record switch and a normal source line link. Confirm actual browser clicks from record detail reached through Table, Graph and Notes, plus Back/Forward/reload and a large attachment window. These checks concern the changed link path, not another broad browser survey. No images, raw HTML, unsafe URL schemes, local filesystem reads or broader preview authority.\n\nUse request/inline-evidence-links from then-current main. Publish exact-path artifacts, obtain independent Architecture/Security/Simplification review of the exact head, update the architecture reference if its contract changes, ratify approval, seal the merge, push main/workroom, verify appropriate CI and remove the owned branch/worktree. This request is source delivery only; any later reader deployment remains a separate operational assignment.","body":{"branch":"request/inline-evidence-links","conditions":"Make record prose/body references to its signed evidence open the correct preview consistently with the evidence list; deterministic source/evidence collisions, bounded metadata, safe record switching, source/history/security preservation, focused regression and actual-browser proof, independent exact-head landing/push/CI/cleanup.","head":"b23c0263033b1d57e7a493d7c30b1ea6c53b980c","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:4a2e1cad18c29df2e827293210ac07cd41cb40b6, g